# The generator's ONLY output is temper/generated/** (plus the
# .openapi-generator/ manifest).
#
# Everything below is hand-written and must never be overwritten. The skin lives
# OUTSIDE the generated package, so this file is defense-in-depth, not the only
# thing standing between `generate-temper-py.sh` and your code.
#
# `temper/__init__.py` is the ONE path where the two trees touch. The generator
# emits an empty namespace __init__ there because `packageName=temper.generated`
# makes `temper` its parent package; ours is the SDK's public surface. Without
# this line every regeneration would silently empty the client's exports — the
# gem has no equivalent hazard, because Ruby's generated tree is reached through
# a `generated.rb` aggregator rather than through a shared parent directory.
temper/__init__.py

# Packaging, tooling and prose: all hand-written, none of it generated.
pyproject.toml
setup.py
setup.cfg
requirements.txt
test-requirements.txt
tox.ini
README.md
git_push.sh
.gitignore
.gitlab-ci.yml
.travis.yml
.github/**

# The generator's own pytest scaffolding (`test/`) and per-model markdown
# (`docs/`) are ~1200 files of no-op stubs. The gem drops both for the same
# reason: hand-written tests live in `tests/`, and the contract's own
# documentation is openapi.json.
test/**
docs/**
